window.POSGuideSearchIndex = [{"title": "Introduction", "order": 1, "filename": "01-introduction.html", "text": "Introduction NLI POS is a browser based point of sale and back office application. You can enter customer orders, record payments, maintain customer and product records, track stock by location, and review sales information. Your account's assigned roles and office access determine which records and pages you can use. Ask your administrator which access applies to your work. Who uses NLI POS Cashiers and customer service staff enter orders, record payments, and look up customers when they have the required access. Store managers review sales and stock information. The application does not define a separate Manager role; an administrator assigns the roles and office access that a manager needs. Inventory staff review stock, record stock changes, move stock between locations, and review inventory transactions. Accounting staff review sales, payment, and report information. Administrators manage users, offices, products, inventory, payment methods, lookup lists, audit logs, and data utilities. The roles configured in the application are Admin , CS , Accounting , and Inventory . The screens available to you can also depend on your assigned office or offices. What you can do Enter and review customer orders and payments. Print or email a receipt from an order. Void an order. Voiding restores the sold stock; a separate return or refund workflow is not available. Maintain customers, products, prices, and inventory, when your access allows it. Review sales reports and the dashboard. The application does not provide a cash drawer shift workflow or a hold and recall workflow. See Voids, Refunds, and Returns, Holding and Recalling Transactions, and Shift and Cash Drawer for details. Screenshot coming soon: Standalone User Guide home page Figure: Standalone User Guide home page (screenshot to be added)"}, {"title": "Getting Started", "order": 2, "filename": "02-getting-started.html", "text": "Getting Started Use a current web browser on your organization's approved network. Ask your administrator for the NLI POS web address and the account credentials issued to you. Sign in 1. Open the NLI POS web address provided by your administrator. Expected result: The sign in page appears. 2. Enter your account email in Email . Expected result: Your email appears in the field. 3. Enter your password in Password . Expected result: Your password is hidden in the field. 4. Select Remember me? only on a trusted, private device. Expected result: The app may remember your sign in on this device. 5. Select Log In . Expected result: The application opens the home page or the page you requested. If you cannot sign in, check the web address and account details. Use Forgot your password? if it is available for your account, or ask your administrator for help. NLI POS sign in page with account fields concealed Figure: Enter your account credentials; the example sign in values are concealed. Find your way around 1. After signing in, open the left navigation. On a tablet or smaller screen, open Menu first. Expected result: The navigation links appear. 2. Select Home for shortcuts or Dashboard for sales indicators and charts. 3. Select Order to find orders or start a sale, and Customer to find customer records. 4. Open Reports to choose a sales report. 5. If you are an administrator, open Settings to manage users and store setup. 6. Select Help at any time to browse this guide. Expected result: This guide opens in a new browser tab. 7. Open the signed in user menu to select Manage Account or Logout . NLI POS home page and navigation Figure: Use Home and the left navigation to reach the main work areas. Review your account 1. Open the signed in user menu and select Manage Account . Expected result: Your account page opens. 2. Choose Profile , Email , or Password in the account navigation. 3. Update the fields on the selected page and save the change. Expected result: A message confirms whether the update succeeded. 4. Select Logout when you finish on a shared device. First time access 1. Ask your administrator to confirm that your account is active and has the correct role. Expected result: Your account can open the pages required for your work. 2. Confirm that you have access to the office or offices where you work. Expected result: Your assigned office appears in the relevant lists. 3. Ask your administrator to confirm that the required products, prices, stock, customer classes, and payment methods are available. Expected result: The options you need are available when you enter an order. Manage Account profile page with account details concealed Figure: Manage Account shows profile and account options; personal details are concealed."}, {"title": "Making a Sale", "order": 3, "filename": "03-making-a-sale.html", "text": "Making a Sale Use Order to create an order, add products, record one or more payment methods, and save the sale. Enter the order 1. Select Order in the navigation. Expected result: The Orders list opens. 2. Select New Order . Expected result: The New Order form appears. 3. Choose the correct Office and Order Date . Expected result: The order is associated with the selected office and date. 4. Select Search Customer , search by name, customer ID, email, or mobile number, and choose the matching customer. Expected result: The customer's name and class appear on the order. 5. If the customer is not listed, select New Customer , complete the required fields, and save the customer. Expected result: The customer record is saved and can be selected on the order. 6. Choose a Category : Regular , Promo/Package , or Freebie . Expected result: The product list reflects the selected category. 7. Choose a Product . For a package, choose Promo Product or Combination (if applicable) . Expected result: The selected item and available price appear. 8. Enter Quantity and select Add to Cart . Expected result: The item appears in Cart , and the amount due updates. 9. Repeat product selection and Add to Cart for each item. New Order form Figure: Enter the office, customer, products, quantities, payment, and salesperson on New Order. Take payment and place the order 1. Under Payment , choose a Method and enter the payment Amount . Expected result: The payment row shows the selected tender and amount. 2. Enter a Ref No. when the payment method requires a reference. Expected result: The reference appears on the payment row. 3. Add another payment row if the customer uses more than one method. Expected result: Each tender appears as a separate payment line. 4. Choose the required Sales By person. Choose a Sales Source or enter Notes when needed. Expected result: The order contains the selected salesperson and any optional sale details. 5. Check that the payment total is at least Total Amount Due . Expected result: The payment covers the displayed amount. 6. Select Place Order and confirm the prompt. Expected result: The order is saved, a receipt is available from its details, and stock is reduced for the items sold. Discounts, taxes, and charges The order form does not provide a general manual discount or tax entry field. Product prices and package pricing come from the product setup. A payment method may have a configured service charge; review the charge shown on the payment row before placing the order. For receipt and reprint steps, see Receipts. Payment rows with transaction values concealed Figure: Review payment methods, amounts, charges, and references; example transaction values are concealed."}, {"title": "Receipts", "order": 4, "filename": "04-receipts.html", "text": "Receipts You can open a receipt from an order's details, print it through your browser, or email it when the email action is available. Open and print a receipt 1. Select Order and find the order in the Orders list. Use the office filter or search field if needed. Expected result: The matching order appears in the list. 2. Open the order's details. Expected result: Order Details shows the customer, items, totals, and payment summary. 3. Select View Receipt . Expected result: The receipt opens in a separate window. 4. Select Print . Expected result: Your browser's print dialog opens. 5. Choose an available printer and print settings, then confirm printing. Expected result: The browser sends the receipt to the selected printer. Orders list with customer and transaction data concealed Figure: Find a saved order in the Orders list; customer and transaction details are concealed. Order Details page with customer and transaction data concealed Figure: Review a saved order before opening its receipt; customer and transaction details are concealed. Reprint a receipt 1. Find and reopen the saved, non void order. 2. Select View Receipt , then Print . Expected result: The receipt is ready to print again. Email a receipt 1. Open the order details and select View Receipt . 2. Select Email , enter the recipient's email address when prompted, and confirm. Expected result: The page reports whether the email was sent. If receipt email reports an error, check the address and ask your administrator whether email service is available. Use Print if you need a paper copy. The application does not provide a receipt format or printer setup page. Printing uses the browser's print dialog. Receipt preview with customer and purchase data concealed Figure: Open a saved order's receipt to print or email it; purchase details are concealed."}, {"title": "Voids, Refunds, and Returns", "order": 5, "filename": "05-voids-refunds-and-returns.html", "text": "Voids, Refunds, and Returns NLI POS provides Void Order for an order. It does not provide a separate return, exchange, or refund transaction. Void an order 1. Select Order and find the order. Expected result: The matching order appears in the list. 2. Open the order details. Expected result: The order and its items are shown for review. 3. Confirm that you have the correct order and follow your store's approval procedure. Expected result: You are ready to void only the intended order. 4. Select Void Order and confirm the prompt. Expected result: The order is marked void and its sold stock is returned to inventory. Warning: Voiding changes the order and stock records. NLI POS does not provide an unvoid action. Process money returned to a customer according to your store's payment provider procedure. Returns and refunds There is no separate return or refund screen. If a customer returns an item or needs money returned, follow your store's procedure outside NLI POS. Do not use Void Order unless the entire original order should be voided. See Making a Sale for order entry and Receipts for locating a transaction. Screenshot coming soon: Order Details and Void Order confirmation Figure: Review the correct order before confirming a void (screenshot to be added)"}, {"title": "Holding and Recalling Transactions", "order": 6, "filename": "06-holding-and-recalling-transactions.html", "text": "Holding and Recalling Transactions NLI POS does not include a Hold action, a Recall action, or a list of held orders. If checkout cannot be completed 1. Do not leave an unfinished order open expecting another cashier or shift to retrieve it. Expected result: You do not rely on NLI POS to save a held transaction. 2. Follow your store's procedure for an interrupted checkout. Expected result: Staff know how to resume or restart the checkout outside a held orders feature. 3. If you have already placed the order and need to correct it, ask an authorized manager or administrator to review the order and available Void Order action. Expected result: The team follows the store's correction process without relying on a held order feature. Screenshot coming soon: Held transactions list Figure: NLI POS does not have a held transactions list (screenshot to be added)"}, {"title": "Shift and Cash Drawer", "order": 7, "filename": "07-shift-and-cash-drawer.html", "text": "Shift and Cash Drawer NLI POS does not provide a shift opening, drawer opening, cash count, or shift closing workflow. The application does not record an opening balance or a counted closing balance. Review recorded sales 1. Select Reports Daily Sales . Expected result: The Daily Sales report opens. 2. Choose the correct Office and Date . Expected result: The report is set to the office and date you need to review. 3. Select Filter . Expected result: The report shows the sales recorded for the selected office and date. 4. Compare the report with your store's separately recorded drawer count. Expected result: You can review NLI POS sales, but the report does not represent a cash count or drawer reconciliation. Use your store's separate cash handling process to open, count, and close the drawer. Screenshot coming soon: Daily Sales report used alongside a separate drawer count Figure: Daily Sales shows recorded sales; it does not open or close a cash drawer (screenshot to be added)"}, {"title": "Products and Inventory", "order": 8, "filename": "08-products-and-inventory.html", "text": "Products and Inventory Product and stock setup affects checkout. Use only the offices and locations assigned to your work. The Settings menu is visible to administrators; inventory access may also depend on your role and office access. Add or update a product Products list with live product records concealed Figure: Search the Products list and open a product to view or edit; product records are concealed. 1. Open Settings Products . Expected result: The Products list opens. 2. Select Add New to create a product, or choose the edit action beside a product. Expected result: The product form opens. 3. Choose the Product Class , Product Type , and Category . Expected result: The product is assigned the appropriate grouping. 4. Enter the Product Code , Product Name , and any description. Expected result: The product identity is filled in. 5. Choose the price country and enter the applicable price fields, such as Regular , Standard Dist , Staff , BPP , or Med Pack . Expected result: The product has the prices needed by its customer classes. 6. Set Active , Freebie Available , and Staff Available as appropriate. Expected result: Product availability matches the store's setup. 7. Select Save . Expected result: The product or product changes are saved. The Products list includes search and export or print actions. Promo/Package products may have combinations that identify their component products and quantities. Product details form with product and price values concealed Figure: Review product classification, prices, and availability; live product values are concealed. Edit Product form with product and price values concealed Figure: Edit product details and customer class prices; live product values are concealed. Package product form with product and price values concealed Figure: Review package components and promo settings; live product values are concealed. New Product form Figure: Set product classification, prices, and availability before saving. Review and record stock 1. Open Settings Inventory . 2. Choose Warehouse , Stockroom , or Offices in the inventory navigation. Expected result: The selected location's inventory list appears. 3. Review the product's stock quantity and minimum level. 4. To record stock, select Add New , choose the Location and Product , enter Stock Quantity and Minimum Level , and add Remarks if needed. Expected result: The stock entry is ready to save. 5. Select Save . Expected result: The stock record is saved for the selected location. Warehouse inventory list with live stock data concealed Figure: Review warehouse stock and minimum levels; live product and quantity data are concealed. Office inventory list with live stock data concealed Figure: Review stock for an office; live product and quantity data are concealed. Stockroom inventory list with live stock data concealed Figure: Review stock for a stockroom; live product and quantity data are concealed. Add Inventory Stock form with selected values concealed Figure: Record a stock quantity and minimum level; the example location and product are concealed. Transfer stock 1. Open the relevant inventory list and choose the product's transfer action. Expected result: The Stock Transfer form opens. 2. Choose the From and To locations. Expected result: The transfer identifies the source and destination. 3. Enter the Quantity and any Remarks . Expected result: The transfer contains the quantity to move and any note. 4. Select Transfer . Expected result: Stock moves between locations and the transfer is recorded. Locations, transactions, and conversions Use Locations to add or edit a location's Name , Location Type , and optional Office . Use Transactions to review recorded stock movements by date, type, product, location, quantity, and user. Use Conversion to manage rules connecting a From Product , To Product , and conversion Quantity . Stock Transfer form with live location and product values concealed Figure: Choose source and destination locations and enter a quantity; example values are concealed. Screenshot coming soon: Inventory Locations Figure: Review warehouse, stockroom, and office inventory locations (screenshot to be added) Inventory transaction history with live records concealed Figure: Review stock movements by date, product, location, and user; live records are concealed. Product conversion rules with live product values concealed Figure: Review product conversion rules; the example product names and quantities are concealed. Add Conversion Rule form with selected values concealed Figure: Enter a source product, destination product, and conversion quantity; example values are concealed."}, {"title": "Customers", "order": 9, "filename": "09-customers.html", "text": "Customers Use Customer to search for a customer, review their profile, or register a new customer. Find a customer 1. Select Customer in the navigation. Expected result: The Customers list opens. 2. Enter a name or other search text in Search... , or choose a country filter. Expected result: The list narrows to matching records. 3. Open the customer's details. Expected result: The customer profile appears. 4. Choose Customer Information or Order History to review the profile or recorded orders. Customers list with customer records concealed Figure: Search or filter customers from the Customers list; personal records are concealed. Screenshot coming soon: Customer profile and Order History Figure: Review customer information and the orders recorded for that customer (screenshot to be added) Register a customer 1. In Customer , select New Customer . Expected result: Customer Registration opens. 2. Choose Customer Class and Office . Expected result: The customer is associated with the right class and office. 3. Enter the required First Name , Last Name , Gender , Birthday , and Civil Status . Expected result: The required personal information is complete. 4. Choose Country and enter any available contact or address details. Expected result: The contact and address information is ready to save. 5. Select Save . Expected result: The customer is saved and can be selected for an order. Customer Registration form Figure: Complete the required identity, customer class, office, and country fields. During checkout, you can also open Search Customer and select New Customer . Search by name, customer ID, email, or mobile number to find an existing record. Search Customer dialog with search text and results concealed Figure: Search for an existing customer before creating a new record; personal details are concealed. Use the edit and details actions on the customer list to maintain a profile. Deletion availability depends on the access assigned to your account."}, {"title": "Reports and Reading Them", "order": 10, "filename": "10-reports-and-reading-them.html", "text": "Reports and Reading Them Reports help you review recorded sales and salesperson targets. Choose the correct Office and reporting period before comparing results. A report with no rows may have no matching activity or the wrong filters. Dashboard The Dashboard shows total sales, order count, average order value, and charts for sales trends, products, salespeople, customers, staff purchases, and payment methods. Choose Office , Start Date , and End Date , then select Apply Filters . Use chart controls where shown to change the category or comparison period. Sales Dashboard with live sales and employee data concealed Figure: Review sales indicators and charts; live sales and employee data are concealed. Daily Sales 1. Open Reports Daily Sales . Expected result: The Daily Sales report opens. 2. Choose an Office and Date . Expected result: The report is set to the period you want to review. 3. Select Filter . Expected result: The report shows order and product detail rows for that date. 4. Review the order number, customer, product, quantity, payment method, and reference information. Compare the totals at the bottom of the table. Screenshot coming soon: Daily Sales report and date filter Figure: Filter Daily Sales by office and date, then review the matching sales lines (screenshot to be added) Sales by Date Range 1. Open Reports Sales by Date Range . Expected result: The report opens. 2. Choose an Office , Date From , and Date To . Expected result: The report is set to the selected office and date range. 3. Select Filter . Expected result: The report shows sales lines in the selected period. 4. Review the order, customer, product, quantity, amount, payment, and encoding columns. Screenshot coming soon: Sales by Date Range report Figure: Review order and payment details for the selected office and date range (screenshot to be added) Monthly Sales 1. Open Reports Monthly Sales . Expected result: The Monthly Sales report opens. 2. Choose an Office , Month , and Year . Expected result: The report is set to the selected month and year. 3. Select Filter . Expected result: The monthly sales report displays the selected period. 4. Select Export to Excel to download the displayed report when needed. Screenshot coming soon: Monthly Sales report filters and results Figure: Choose the office, month, and year before reviewing or exporting Monthly Sales (screenshot to be added) Order Details 1. Open Reports Order Details . Expected result: The Order Details report opens. 2. Choose an Office , Month , and Year , then select Filter . Expected result: Purchases lists orders for the selected period. 3. Select an order in Purchases . Expected result: Details shows the customer, date, remarks, products, quantities, and total. 4. Select Export to Excel to download the filtered report. Order Details report with customer and transaction data concealed Figure: Select a purchase to review the order and its line items; live records are concealed. Sales Quota 1. Open Reports Sales Quota and choose an Office . Expected result: The quota list is filtered to the selected office. 2. Select Add Sales Quota or the edit action beside a quota. Expected result: The quota form opens. 3. Choose the Salesperson and Year and Month , then enter the Quota Amount . Expected result: The quota target is ready to save for that salesperson and period. 4. Select Save Quota . Expected result: The list shows month to date sales, quota amount, variance, and achieved percentage. Screenshot coming soon: Sales Quota results Figure: Compare each salesperson's month to date sales with the quota (screenshot to be added) There is no separate end of day cash drawer or shift close report. Daily Sales shows sales recorded in NLI POS; use your store's cash count procedure to reconcile a drawer."}, {"title": "Users, Roles, and Settings", "order": 11, "filename": "11-users-roles-and-settings.html", "text": "Users, Roles, and Settings The Settings menu is available to administrators. Your assigned role and office access determine which pages and records you can use. Manage users and access 1. Open Settings Users . Expected result: The user list appears. 2. Open the user record you need to manage. 3. Assign the required role or roles and office access. Expected result: The saved user account reflects the assigned access. 4. Ask the user to sign in again if their access does not appear to have changed. The configured roles are Admin , CS , Accounting , and Inventory . The application does not include a separate Manager role. User role and access settings with account details concealed Figure: Assign only the role and office access the user needs; account details are concealed. User office access with identity and office data concealed Figure: Review assigned office access; identity and office names are concealed. Users list with personal account records concealed Figure: Open an account from the Users list; personal account data is concealed. Maintain offices and setup lists Use Offices to maintain office details, country, and active status. Office settings supply regional details used by the application. Use Sales Sources to manage the choices available when recording an order. Use Utilities Payment Methods to maintain the method name, description, Service Charge (%) , and active status. Only active methods are offered during order entry. Use Customer Classes and product price fields to maintain customer specific pricing. Use Product Types and Countries to maintain corresponding form choices. Use Background to choose an application background and Themes to select Default , Pulse , Flatly , or Lumen . Use Audit Logs to review recorded activity. Sales Sources settings Figure: Administrators maintain the sales sources offered on an order. Screenshot coming soon: Payment Methods setup Figure: Review a payment method's name, service charge, and active status (screenshot to be added) Export data and backups 1. Open Settings Utilities Backup . Expected result: Export Table to CSV opens. 2. Choose a table in Select a table: and select Export CSV . Expected result: The selected table downloads as a CSV file. A separate administrator only Database Backup page provides Backup Now and Download Backup ; it is not linked from the current sidebar. Ask your administrator if you need to use it. Screenshot coming soon: Office settings Figure: Maintain office details and the regional settings used by the application (screenshot to be added) Screenshot coming soon: Administrator utilities Figure: Review lookup lists, appearance settings, audit logs, and export tools (screenshot to be added) There are no tax configuration, receipt format, or printer setup pages in the application. Receipt printing uses the browser print dialog."}, {"title": "Troubleshooting and FAQ", "order": 12, "filename": "12-troubleshooting-and-faq.html", "text": "Troubleshooting and FAQ Use the steps below to resolve common validation messages. If an issue continues, note the page, action, and exact message and contact your administrator. Sale validation messages Message or problem What to do “Please select a customer.” Choose a customer before adding an item to the cart. “Please select a product.” Choose a product before selecting Add to Cart . “Please select a promo product or combination.” For a Promo/Package sale, choose Promo Product or Combination (if applicable) . “Price is not set for this product.” Ask an administrator to review the product price for the selected customer class and country. “Not enough stock for …” Check available stock for the product or package component. Reduce the quantity or ask inventory staff to correct the stock record. Payment is less than the order total. Add or correct payment rows until the total is at least Total Amount Due . “Please select a Sales Person before placing the order.” Choose a person in Sales By , then place the order again. Other common problems Required fields on Customer Registration: Complete the fields marked required, including Customer Class , Office , First Name , Last Name , Gender , Birthday , Civil Status , and Country . A page is missing or access is denied: Ask an administrator to check that your account is active and has the required role and office access. A report is empty: Check the selected office and date or month, then select Filter again. Receipt email reports an error: Check the recipient address and ask your administrator whether receipt email service is available. Use Print as an alternative. A page keeps loading or results do not update: Check your network, refresh the page, and repeat the action. If it continues, report the page and message to your administrator. Screenshot coming soon: Order form showing a validation message Figure: Correct the highlighted field or order requirement before trying again (screenshot to be added) Frequently asked questions Can I put a transaction on hold and finish it later? No. NLI POS does not have a hold and recall workflow. Follow your store's procedure for an interrupted checkout. Can I record a refund or product return? No. The available order action is Void Order . Follow your store's separate return and refund process. Where do I open or close the cash drawer? NLI POS does not track drawer counts or shift opening and closing. Use your store's cash handling procedure. Can I add a discount or tax to an order? The order entry screen has no general discount or tax field. Product prices and configured package pricing determine the displayed amounts."}, {"title": "Glossary", "order": 13, "filename": "13-glossary.html", "text": "Glossary Term Meaning in NLI POS Office A store or branch selected when entering orders and filtering information. Customer class A customer category used with product price setup. Product class The product grouping Main or Collateral . Category A sale grouping such as Regular , Promo/Package , or Freebie . Combination A configured set of component products used by a package. Payment method The configured tender type selected on an order, such as cash or another enabled method. Service charge A charge rate configured for a payment method and displayed on its payment row when applicable. Sales source The recorded source or reason for a sale, chosen from the configured list. Void A status applied to an order using Void Order ; the application restores the sold stock. Stockroom / warehouse Inventory locations used to organize stock. Conversion rule A configured relationship between a source product, destination product, and quantity. Minimum level A stock threshold recorded for a product at a location. Office access The list of offices a user account is allowed to work with."}];
